[{:db/id -1 :adr/id "adr-2609161808-cloud-kotoba-org-repos-transfer" :adr/title "Move kotoba cloud repositories to the cloud-kotoba org" :adr/status :accepted :adr/body "Owner created the cloud-kotoba organization and requested the kotoba cloud surface move out of the kotoba-lang language-substrate org. Transfer kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud and kotoba-lang/cloud-kotoba-dds to cloud-kotoba (the only two repositories matching the cloud-kotoba surface; kotoba-lang holds 2754 repositories and the rest stays as the language substrate). GitHub keeps redirects from the old names. Update manifest/repos.edn: new remote cloud-kotoba, +cloud-kotoba in group-filter, org role :cloud-operator in :orgs, and old-to-new entries in :path-overrides so stale path candidates (extra-projects, docs) resolve. Regenerate manifest/west.yml with --entry for exactly the two repositories; pins are unchanged (67603d12, 22cefcd). Absorb the same change in manifest/fleet-db.edn (header rebuilt from west.yml, remotes vector, the two repo records) with no new reconcile drift. Move the local checkouts to orgs/cloud-kotoba/, set-url the remotes, and regenerate .gitignore via gen-orgs-gitignore. Live cron jobs.json and profile SOUL.md files are path-patched in place; the repo cron ledger is re-exported from live. Historical ADRs and dated reports keep their old paths as written."}]